WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.870
-My first guest is a six-time
Grammy nominated artist.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.972
He's one of the best dudes
on Earth.

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:09.409
His new show, "Post Malone's
Celebrity World Pong League,"

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.177
premieres November 18th

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:14.013
on Messenger's new
Watch Together feature.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:18.251
Here is Post Malone! Posty!
-Hello, everybody.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.853
-Yeah.
-What's going on, bubba?

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:23.055
-You look good, bud.
You look great, actually.

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:25.725
Where are you right now, pal?

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.127
-I'm home in Utah right now.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.296
-Utah?
-Kind of just relaxing

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.431
and trying to stay
out of trouble.

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:33.833
You know?
-Yeah.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.803
You're like in
the mountain air and --

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:40.273
-Feels good. You know, I smoke
too much, too.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:43.309
So the air really gets to me.
So I like -- [ Deep breath ]

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:47.013
Every time I go up a set of
stairs, I can't --

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.449
-Yeah, you learn a
lesson every time you breathe.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:52.652
-Yes, sir, I suppose.
-Have you been --

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.788
I know you probably have,
you can't stop.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.388
Have you been working
on new music?

00:00:56.388 --> 00:01:00.826
-Yes, sir.
You know, it's --

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:04.029
it's been a while, you know,
getting into the studio

00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:06.532
and stuff after, you know, kind
of -- I remember the beginning

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:08.434
of the whole COVID thing,
and then

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:11.504
when they finally opened up the
studio so I could go in

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:15.642
and work, and lately
I've just been, you know,

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:18.110
trying to mess around and
make some cool stuff

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.945
and some funky stuff.

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:22.614
And I think we're making some
awesome stuff right now.

00:01:22.614 --> 00:01:25.752
-As a songwriter, is it
harder to make music during

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.554
a time like this, or does this
kind of push you

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:30.723
to actually make music?
-I don't know.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:34.026
I suppose, you know, maybe not
harder, but maybe different.

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:37.864
Like I've had more time to be,
I guess, introspective.

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:40.433
You know, kind of not being able
to go out.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.835
-Hey, Post, I'm sorry,
I think there's a burglar

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.470
trying to
break into your house.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.839
-Oh, yeah, these guys --
I don't know,

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:48.974
they just hang around
the house.

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:52.478
-You pay them to
break into your house?

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:54.213
-Dude, you ruined the bit.

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:56.316
This was supposed to be the
whole bit for the show.

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.617
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.951
-It's almost like Cato.

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:01.254
-We'll give them the guest
house over there, so...

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.988
-You pay them to break
in just to make sure

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:06.492
your security system works.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.060
Dude, I like --
-Worst guest of all time.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.563
He looked cool, man.
He's got no face.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.898
He's like --
Dude, I like that character,

00:02:12.898 --> 00:02:14.968
man, no face.
That guy scared me.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.002
Man, he was rad.

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:19.438
Hey, I want to talk about your
new show, it's called

00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:22.241
"Post Malone's
Celebrity World Pong League."

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.776
-Sure.
-It premieres next week on

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:27.013
Messenger's new Watch Together
feature.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:29.048
Which is a really fun feature,
by the way.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:31.251
What made you think
of this idea?

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:34.587
-Umm, I guess just being
drunk, playing beer pong.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:37.456
You know, I figured eventually
we want to kind of

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:42.128
make it like a league and do
like -- I don't --

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:45.465
maybe not arenas off rip,
but like middle school

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:48.234
basketball courts.
-[ Laughs ] Yeah?

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.902
-I'm sure...
-You know, small-scale

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:53.239
type deal, but I want to make it
every city has a team,

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:56.175
where like the best
schools, you know,

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.010
the best beer pong players
from each school

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.746
have a team and it's a whole
bracket like the NFL

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:02.514
or the NBA
or something.

00:03:02.514 --> 00:03:04.683
That's down the line.
You know, but this show

00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:07.520
is more about just
kicking it with a couple of

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.190
friends and just, you know,
talking, shooting the breeze,

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.759
and just playing beer pong,
getting a little drunk,

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:15.694
you know.
It's a lot of fun.

00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:18.631
-I heard a story, and
it has to be true,

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:21.433
but did you challenge
Patrick Mahomes,

00:03:21.433 --> 00:03:24.770
Super Bowl MVP Patrick Mahomes,

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.339
to a game of beer pong,
and what went actually down?

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:29.675
And was there a bet?

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:32.612
-Yeah. He challenged me,

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:35.814
and I was so game and I was
like, "Let's go."

00:03:35.814 --> 00:03:38.685
We were backstage,
I think we were in KC,

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:41.453
but we were backstage,
and Patrick Mahomes

00:03:41.453 --> 00:03:43.656
and Travis Kelce walk in
and they were like,

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.691
"Let's play some pong."

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:47.626
They had just won
the Super Bowl.

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:50.263
And I'm like, well, you know,
there's no way

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:52.632
I'm going to say no
because in actuality,

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:56.068
I'm the best player, I know.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:58.504
-But you know, we got down
the line a couple games,

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.873
and I was starting to get drunk
and they get beating us

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.742
and beating us and beating us.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.543
And then I was like,
"You know what?

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:06.979
Let's keep playing.

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:11.017
And if you win,
I'll get a tattoo

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.386
of a Kansas City Chiefs logo,

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:17.456
and y'all's autograph
on my arm, as well."

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:19.658
-Their autographs?

00:04:19.658 --> 00:04:21.193
-Yeah, you want to see it?

00:04:21.193 --> 00:04:23.996
-I can't believe you
did this, man.

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:26.298
Dude, this is --

00:04:26.298 --> 00:04:27.967
Oh, my gosh. Wait. Move --

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.602
-That's the good stuff
right there.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:33.439
-Oh, my gosh.
-This is on me forever.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.308
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:37.810
-Only you would do that.
That is so funny, man.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.945
Did they freak out?
Did they freak out?

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:41.914
-Yeah, he was like, "You don't
have to really do it."

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.816
And I was like,
"Oh, come on, man,

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.818
let me do it.
I told you I would do it."

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.052
-"I told you,
I'm a man of my word.

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:48.654
I'm a man of my word."

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.423
-Jimmy, will you say hi
to my stepmom?

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:52.324
-Yeah. Please.
I would love to.

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:55.961
I would be honored.
Yeah. Mom?

00:04:55.961 --> 00:04:58.064
Where's stepmom?
-You're always meeting moms.

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:01.067
-I know.
-The moms dig you.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.268
-Yeah.
-This is Jodie.

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:04.103
-Oh, come on.
What, are you kidding me?

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:06.872
Hi, nice to -- come on!
Nice to meet you.

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:08.541
Are you having fun out there
in Utah?

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:11.777
-We love Utah.
Great, great time.

00:05:11.777 --> 00:05:14.680
-It really is good. All right,
good. Stay safe, okay?

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.749
-Thanks, you too.
-I love you, Jodie.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.618
-Are you kidding me?
Dude, how cute.

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:20.853
That's so fun.
-She's the best.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:24.524
-You played beer pong against
a lot of famous people.

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.625
Is there anyone else that
we'd be surprised to learn

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:29.328
isn't really that good?

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:32.365
-Umm, trying to think.

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:35.133
I played with K.D.,
I played with Kevin Durant.

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:37.202
-He's not good?
-He was good.

00:05:37.202 --> 00:05:38.504
Yeah, but he's a cheater,

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.339
because his wingspan is like
ten feet.

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.842
-He's a leaner.
-His elbows were always

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:45.044
over the table every time.
-Yeah, no, no, no.

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:47.146
That's cheat--
Yeah, no, no, no. I don't --

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:49.214
Dude, no, you gotta
know the rules.

00:05:49.214 --> 00:05:51.884
-You can't help it, though.
You know --

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:53.252
If you're so -- you're so --

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.221
Your wingspan is just
so long, you can't help it.

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:57.556
-You can't dunk the ball.
-Drake's no good.

00:05:57.556 --> 00:06:00.326
Drake's no good.
-Where did you play Drake?

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:03.229
-In Toronto, I think.
-Home court.

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:06.198
-He came backstage
at the show in Toronto,

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:09.168
and we started playing
beer pong.

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:12.170
And I was just like,
man, he sucks.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:14.206
-"Dude, you're terrible."

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:19.511
-If you see this, come meet me
again, we'll play again.

00:06:19.511 --> 00:06:21.080
But he was terrible.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:24.350
-You've beaten me before
in beer pong, and I was happy.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:28.054
I was actually -- it was a badge
of honor to lose to you.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:29.855
But I have an idea
for a rematch.

00:06:29.855 --> 00:06:33.159
What if you and I competed
in every drinking game ever

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:35.361
in one game?
-I'm ready to go.

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:37.063
-Post Malone and I are
going head to head...

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:38.664
-Let me know.
-...in every drinking game ever,

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:39.798
when we come back.

00:06:39.798 --> 00:06:41.401
More "Tonight Show."
Stick around.

